Z||000000||Blaster||07-27-2000||03:28 AM||||This was a problem I had awhile back. I went to a local performance shop and bought an accell coil.  I drove the car for about 2 days and it was fine.  Then on the third day, on my way home, my car lost all power and started back firing.  It died on me.  Waited a couple mins and started it back up.  It would idle alright, but if I touched the gas it would eat it.  Called a friend and he brought me my stock coil.  Threw it in there and it started right up and ran ok again.  I drove it home and threw the accell back in there and it started doing that backfiring crap again.  I went back to the shop I got it from, had to go through a bunch of hassle with them, and they gave me another one.  Drove it to a friends house a installed it.  Drove about two miles and it started the backfiring again and died.  Threw the stock one back in and it ran ok.  Now I went back to the shop and the owner could not figure out what it was. They put a tester on it and said everything looked alright.  Finally I got my money back and just gave up.  <BR>Now the only thing I could think of is that it was retarding my timing. I have 8mm superstock wires on there, and I am sure they could handle it, and I run ACDelco Rapid fires. I thought maybe it was sending bad signals, but to get 2 new coils that both sent bad signals would be a long shot.  No one around here that I know could come up with a reason other than the timing being retarded.  I was thinking about going with the MSD coil, but I don't want to go through the same thing.  Has anyone else had any similar problems like this?  Sorry for the long post. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||5
